{"id":"H2956","lemma":"טָרַד","transliteration":"tarad","sayIt":"ta-RAD","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to pursue","meaning":"1) to pursue, chase, be continuous\n1a) (Qal) dripping (participle)\nAramaic equivalent: te.rad (טְרַד \"to chase away\" H2957)","glosses":["constant"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"pro-19","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"is like a constant","kjv":"are a continual"}},{"chapterId":"pro-27","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"A constant","kjv":"A continual"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Proverbs 19:13","note":"A foolish son is the calamity of his father. A wife’s quarrels are a continual dripping.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H2957","lemma":"טְרַד","transliteration":"terad","gloss":"to chase away"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}